<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Rights groups oppose UAE’s Lana Nusseibeh for UN chief over Sudan claims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61ea9fc9ec25394c7de20c9f4296b1d821e5243a7171cac0993bb64522b4545a</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T02:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-lana-nusseibeh-un-chief-uae-sudan-rights-groups" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups on Tuesday urged countries to reject UAE diplomat Lana Nusseibeh’s bid to become UN secretary general citing allegations that Abu Dhabi funds Sudan’s paramilitary Rapid Support Forces. The UAE denies the accusations. Nusseibeh, 48, is seeking to become the first woman to lead the United Nations.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles confronts calls for slavery apology during Caribbean tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056ef785beb7f85e67f68ccf5e5077e0d5f907d373bd72d287847b76af097de7</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T23:14:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-king-charles-slavery-apology-caribbean-tour" /><summary type="html">King Charles III began a Caribbean tour in the Bahamas on Tuesday, acknowledging “the great suffering of the past” amid calls for an apology over slavery. The 77-year-old monarch, undergoing cancer treatment, will also visit Guyana and Antigua and Barbuda, highlighting climate threats and attending a Commonwealth summit with Queen Camilla.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's defeated candidate Flavio Bolsonaro flees to US despite cancelled passports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e47d598bc136c6d66b545f2625051ee409496d82957e47dc1ad56bef5fd4808</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown" /><summary type="html">Brazil's former presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro fled to the US, sources said Tuesday, despite his passports being cancelled after he failed to comply with a Supreme Court order to hand them over as part of a money laundering probe. Bolsonaro's whereabouts had been a source of speculation since his election defeat on Sunday to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>USA: Could a Democrat win a statewide election in Texas?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c5d42eb8321e835d259a483c46956ef2748fd27b7440cd39b5992f5412ef11c</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-usa-could-a-democrat-win-a-statewide-election-in-texas" /><summary type="html">There is only one week left until the US midterm elections. In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico, could win a Senate seat for the first time in decades.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Get the Flock out': Americans respond to AI cameras in bipartisan backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d49e267e498c174aba715051972d6d8ca6af47cf2b254073ac1236559dcbcc0f</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midt--835d29b1fccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">AI-driven Flock cameras made by an Atlanta-based company are sprouting up across the US, sparking alarm and bipartisan, citizen-driven campaigns as the new technology emerges as a 2026 midterm campaign issue. While politicians hedge and local officials rush to sign contracts, community volunteers attempt to address an issue with major implications for future generations. But it might be too late.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump escalates anti-Muslim attacks against Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76372775aecdd2cc93bd5e76bb542d5d0ddfb2b3c731f647ecc8b43efda30e83</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:56:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-e--f4a83701aa1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-el-sayed" /><summary type="html">As the US midterm elections approach, the Michigan Senate race is splitting communities. Trump is escalating anti-Muslim attacks against Abdul El-Sayed, the Michigan Democratic Senate candidate, who could become the first Muslim senator in US history.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro vows to lead opposition after Brazil court imposes travel ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27e9845d7c05e9973bb42c22ecb2363fb994dd00269178b002e819f156f3874d</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:56:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban--4575bf06ed5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-flavio-bolsonaro-opposition-brazil-court-travel-ban" /><summary type="html">Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro said on Monday that a Supreme Court justice had barred him from leaving the country after he narrowly lost to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. Bolsonaro, who refused to concede defeat, denounced the order as intimidation and vowed to challenge the election results.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump offers $1 million for tipoffs leading to vote fraud conviction as midterms approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a037b53eeeb749d7987c376d860e0b60b785d80fd24baea44156d50cf493f79</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:17:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach--cb23d5a53a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-trump-offers-1-million-for-tipoffs-leading-to-vote-fraud-conviction-as-midterms-approach" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Monday pledged a $1 million reward for information on voter fraud leading to conviction ahead of the upcoming 2026 US midterms on November 3. The president gave no details of how the reward would be funded or administered. The comments follow his repeated false claims that he won the 2020 presidential election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Comeback kid: How did Brazil's veteran leader Lula upset Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5ee1f57444f94e7c24ab32b0598a510ae5356897ced8042826ed0ce4a26f111</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T19:22:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro--c3955199ecd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Just two days shy of his 81st birthday, Brazil's Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva has emerged as the comeback kid. Coming from behind in the polls after a bitter campaign where he often showed his age, Lula has become the first candidate since Brazil’s return to democracy in the 1980s to win the presidential run-off after trailing in the first round. How did the Workers' Party leader turn a 2.2 million vote deficit against the far right's Flavio Bolsonaro into a 4.4 million vote win? Just three short weeks ago, most races at the federal and state level broke the way of conservatives and the far right.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What does Lula's re-election mean for the Amazon?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f99bf7113ea104c7f4bf9988a8fb06b11e6161806bfb4ce3dfac0dd00210fcbd</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon--6f4fc14c1029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon" /><summary type="html">Climate activists in Brazil are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders across Americas react to Brazil President Lula's re-election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a513fc278e5f997aa0899ecbd2f173579d7853f3be19b74627637bc984b815b</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:05:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election--efc0688d3f0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election" /><summary type="html">​President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won Brazil's presidential election on Sunday (October 25), defeating right-wing ​Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in a runoff to secure a fourth non-consecutive term.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Lula accustomed to negotiating tough bargains': Campaign promises collide with right-wing Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d53a6840a456856363d36941f37114b24bca7aa98ccc7fcd5301ae7eab05dfcb</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:54:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress--662d1f784eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Christopher Sabatini, Director of Chatham House's Latin America Programme. Sabatini examines how Lula's campaign reinvention, youth mobilisation, and the changing dynamics of Bolsonarismo are reshaping Brazil's political landscape. By embracing social media, mobilising younger voters, and shifting attention from his historical achievements to the economic anxieties of ordinary Brazilians, Lula managed to transform the electoral contest. As Sabatini explains, voters were no longer satisfied with hearing about the past. They wanted an answer to a more immediate question: "What are you going to do for us now?</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula's re-election brings hope for the Amazon as deforestation drops to record low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9487546cbb01b92e5bb367e2ac91bfc8f56fd42d9fc8cdeb8a566af72877f060</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261026-lula-s-re-election-brings-hope-for-the-amazon-as-deforestation-drops-to-record-low--5efd7aaf7e54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261026-lula-s-re-election-brings-hope-for-the-amazon-as-deforestation-drops-to-record-low" /><summary type="html">Climate activists in Brazil and beyond are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest, appropriately nicknamed the planet's lungs. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula reelected president in runoff vote: A look back at his career</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8f4e4d6bc2a4eab5f0bad1a1e30ced4c18b4919c399ad60201377dfdff21ec7</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:11:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career--7ab7020c363f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term on Sunday (October 25), the country's electoral court said, in a shock result that defied polls.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms 2026: A history of gerrymandering</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb4094f2907c8b0774ee3ed803aeb56c9722b577995978f730a718dbc08a3b3</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:48:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering--2a4bc0975c37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering" /><summary type="html">What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:056e6a65a4abbee9b599c5996b1a7be4ea191ce3f346164cef81ac299705726a</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:28:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats--abf7926435d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats" /><summary type="html">Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95dc46b3de28e9bc35308c932a78367c3d66a947d3fe6a355bde7396ad9a3156</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil--6fac97bd28ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf87f1b691b11337107e2d6ac3790df2a7a49c2c9e2e83ae38c51088c4d63e0</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions--61d6451f7b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions" /><summary type="html">Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25eb04da2b3bb28cce718d9c54ea158bd70de016e76928df284248eb644eb109</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:38:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern--90666ecd83fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern" /><summary type="html">Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula beats Bolsonaro in Brazil runoff: What does it mean for Donald Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a7c67607da310c9ff13e9daa116fe8707393255d2d6d380c3c044cd7944b76</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump--db167052dcda.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Lula defeated on Sunday (October 25) Flavio Bolsonaro in Brazil’s presidential election. But rather than conceding, Bolsonaro called for the result to be annulled. As the US midterms approach, the result raises questions about Trump’s influence and how his political allies respond when voters reject them. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Douglas Herbert, gives us his analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Trump's gains among Latino voters in Texas at risk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c26f1902719d18929b56f4955111b875b51fcac7eb3abb7e93e38da65145f2f</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:42:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk--e329d7c95e13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk" /><summary type="html">Latino voters shifted toward Trump two years ago, helping him return to the White House with a Republican-controlled Congress. Now, many are souring on the US president and his party. FRANCE 24's team reports from the Rio Grande Valley.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: What challenges await Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3331721641c947f4e788b8b3dff9e7bff6bd35c6919d99eed2ef86502c145565</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-challenges-await-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president--8878b66b20b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-challenges-await-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). He will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula wins historic fourth term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eea74cb189f36de4fb441c498a1f64f2a73df6cb9ee5ae45a0eaa0f44635fc3b</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:44:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-wins-historic-fourth-term--c42d2b88d359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-wins-historic-fourth-term" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 26). The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula seals re-election in surprise win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f98b225441fdb65919bd08adfd90626b453598e2d0c66e9e03686728536852b7</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:33:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-seals-re-election-in-surprise-win--14bcca65f7eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-seals-re-election-in-surprise-win" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). The far-right candidate and son of former President Jair Bolsonaro has refused to accept the results and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘Congratulations!’: World leaders hail Lula’s election victory in Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c6a6f03a45e099fec1d8c2ccbafd5d49ce6a6176170bc7145cba5fd03b6a170</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T09:31:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-congratulations-world-leaders-hail-lula-s-election-victory-in-brazil--f8a4f4acfab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-congratulations-world-leaders-hail-lula-s-election-victory-in-brazil" /><summary type="html">The international community on Monday congratulated Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva after his stunning re-election in a runoff with right-wing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro. The region's left-leaning leaders were quick to react as Brazil staved off a conservative wave in many countries while Europeans, such as Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez, celebrated a "progressive comeback".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula's 'extraordinary victory' faces growing middle class, deeply-entrenched bolsonarismo &amp; Big Tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f43649588abae816510caa730706ce2f4795fa1666777029fe7b6a6aa1728634</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T08:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-s-extraordinary-victory-faces-growing-middle-class-deeply-entrenched-bolsonarismo-big-tech--7aa8423b656a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-s-extraordinary-victory-faces-growing-middle-class-deeply-entrenched-bolsonarismo-big-tech" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Dr Felipe Krause, Political Scientist, former Diplomat and Departmental Lecturer in Latin American Studies at the Oxford School of Global and Area Studies.  Beneath Lula's electoral triumph lies a more complex political reality: the Brazilian hard right has consolidated its influence across state governments and legislative institutions, raising fundamental questions about the balance of power and the future of progressive governance. Lula will be focusing more on "working to keep things from eroding" rather than advancing his progressive agenda, explains Dr. Krause. 'There is more need for economic measures that support the growing middle class."</summary></entry><entry><title>What challenges await Brazil's Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1f3f0af4bfb156d4d0d35524c5cc5cfbbd09a166f77749006ee141f3bc104de</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T00:52:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-what-challenges-await-brazil-s-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president--877dfdc1d367.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-what-challenges-await-brazil-s-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president" /><summary type="html">President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula beats odds and seals re-election, rival Bolsonaro demands annulment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5626ff7fca679d48635bf09cfa8427ee5c7c900a8b862c6a32fba7ec3fd4795a</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T00:23:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-brazil-s-president-lula-da-silva-beats-flavio-bolsonaro-to-win-re-election--6c66700f9c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-brazil-s-president-lula-da-silva-beats-flavio-bolsonaro-to-win-re-election" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday. The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil presidential election: Lula's late surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaa23862134a120c0e7e2186a4419cae66b9e8ea9bee86b916491101388d7471</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T19:00:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261025-lula-s-legacy-flavio-s-future--edbc5d7dfc1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261025-lula-s-legacy-flavio-s-future" /><summary type="html">It's a coin-flip election in Brazil, with little separating the country's left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro. The results of the run-off vote will become clear in a few hours.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Opposition leader Machado returns to Venezuela after 10 months in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df811598f82ffc3367b34708d99f7ca5d4bf674d03c75283e3752ae639e362f7</id><updated>2026-10-28T05:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T17:10:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-opposition-leader-machado-returns-to-venezuela-after-10-months-in-exile--1872e0f5ffc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-opposition-leader-machado-returns-to-venezuela-after-10-months-in-exile" /><summary type="html">Venezuelan opposition leader Maria Corina Machado announced on Sunday that she has returned to her homeland following almost a year in exile, after covertly leaving Venezuela in late 2025 to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. She returns as doubts about her country’s democratic future and the role of the US are growing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
